## Why This Is Asked
This evaluates understanding of edge cryptography implementation, privacy-preserving design, and business impact analysis in payment systems—skills critical for roles at Cloudflare, Square, and similar fintech companies.

## Key Concepts
- On-device cryptographic verification using Ed25519 and platform crypto APIs
- Key management lifecycle and rotation strategies
- Mobile device constraints: latency, CPU, memory, and energy budgets
- Local telemetry architecture and storage growth patterns
- Regulatory compliance frameworks for payment verification
- Financial modeling with go/no-go criteria and break-even analysis

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: verify an Ed25519 signature on-device
async function verifyReceipt(receipt, publicKey) {
  // receipt: { data: ArrayBuffer, signature: ArrayBuffer }
  const isValid = await crypto.subtle.verify(
    'Ed25519',
    publicKey,
    receipt.signature,
    receipt.data
  );
  return isValid;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to translate a feature into a concrete CBA with privacy constraints, rollout strategy, and measurable ROI.

## Key Concepts

- On-device perceptual hashing
- Memory and CPU budgeting for fingerprint indices
- Data savings vs latency trade-offs
- Privacy/compliance, consent flows
- Rollout plans, offline fallback, drift maintenance, ROI calculation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: fingerprint a media item and decide upload
function shouldUpload(media) {
  const fp = perceptualFingerprint(media);
  const exists = fingerprintIndex.has(fp);
  if (exists) return false;
  fingerprintIndex.add(fp);
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you measure and validate data savings at scale?
- How handle hash collisions and index eviction?
- What telemetry would you collect for ROI without compromising privacy?
